<title>NETHERLANDS: Unilever Q4 net profit NLG 1.15 billion.</title>
<headline>Unilever Q4 net profit NLG 1.15 billion.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM, MONTH 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q4 1996</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (guilders)	   4.10   vs    2.41</p>
<p>    Net profit/current exchange rates     1,153  vs	690</p>
<p>    Net profit/constant exchange rates    1,114  vs	695</p>
<p>    Final Div Unilever NV (guilders)	4.75   vs    4.71</p>
<p>    Total Div Unilever NV (guilders)	6.98   vs    6.19</p>
<p>    Income from fixed investments		40  vs	 47</p>
<p>    Interest charges				137  vs	163</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				1,871  vs    1,044</p>
<p>    Tax						 698  vs	295</p>
<p>    Post-tax profit			     1,173  vs	749</p>
<p>    Minority interests			     59  vs	 54</p>
<p>    Net profit excl. exceptionals	   1,262  vs    1,050</p>
<p>NOTES - Fourth quarter results are stated at constant exchange rates unless otherwise indicated.</p>
<p>Unilever said few conclusions could be drawn from fourth quarter results due to the impact of the different phasing of exceptional items in 1996 as against 1995.</p>
<p>It said fourth quarter net profit in guilders came out 10 percent higher than in the same period of 1995 if exceptional items and lower pension costs were excluded.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
